Create a new workspace from a directory or another workspace

Usage: forkspace new [OPTIONS] [NAME]

Arguments:
  [NAME]  Name for the new workspace (defaults to the source directory's name)

Options:
      --from <SOURCE>      Directory or workspace to start from [default: .]
      --session <SESSION>  Session identifier for grouping related workspaces
      --tmpfs              Keep the workspace's changes in RAM (Linux overlay only; lost on reboot)
      --branch <BRANCH>    Create and record a Git branch in the workspace
      --copy               Consent to a full directory copy backend
      --live               Show later changes to the source in the workspace (Linux overlay only; skips the frozen copy)
  -h, --help               Print help
